> I had the same problem trying to untar it -- it died on the third file
> or so.  Someone here found a workaround -- rename the tar file to
> something else (eg: fred.tar) and it works.  Strange but true.

When you retrieve the compressed tar, don't uncompress it; use
"zcat nethack31.tar.Z | tar xof -", and it'll work fine.  The problem 
is that there's a zero-length file named "nethack31.tar" in the tar file,
and when it extracts, it overwrites the "real" archive and dies, confused.

